IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Tourism Board Act 1963 (Singapore) -- who is a "tourist" and what is "guiding services" (s 20), the tourist guide
-- licence requirement, its exceptions and offences (ss 21, 22), badge surrender (s 25(4)), the Board's sanctions on a guide
-- (s 28(1), (2), (4A)), the cruise terminal licence requirement and the 5% / 25% / 50% controller rules (ss 29A, 29R), the
-- Merlion symbol (s 39), personal immunity (s 37), composition (s 41) and appeal to the Minister (s 42A(1)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/STBA1963.txt. The edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; later amendments are annotated in the text, the latest seen
-- being Act 28 of 2022 (wef 1 April 2023). The deposit's metadata labels it "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
-- The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body for Part 3A; this file follows the BODY's
-- numbers (s 20 interpretation, s 21 licence required, s 22 presumption, s 23 application, s 25 badge, s 28 suspension).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules with decision content that a
-- tourist guide, a business using guides, a cruise terminal operator or investor, or a user of the Merlion meets. Not encoded: the
-- Board's constitution, functions, staff, Tourism Fund (Parts 2, 3), licence applications and conditions beyond the appeal
-- deadline, codes of practice, directions (ss 26, 26A, 26B), the rest of Part 3AA (licence conditions, charges, remedial directions,
-- special administration, winding up), enforcement powers (Part 3B), secrecy (s 35B), and the meanings of "associate", "indirect
-- controller" and "voting power" (ss 29W-29ZA) beyond the percentage thresholds.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Tourism Board Act 1963 -- guides, cruise terminals and the Merlion`

§§ `20 -- tourist and guiding services`

-- s 20(1) "tourist" means an individual who visits Singapore "for recreation, pleasure, business or any other purpose", but does not
-- include (a) a citizen or permanent resident; (b) a work pass holder; (c) a holder of a dependant's pass, student's pass or special
-- pass; (d) a holder of "a visit pass valid for more than 90 days"; (e) a holder of any other pass the Minister specifies by order.
DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `a citizen`
    `a permanent resident`
    `a work pass holder`
    `a dependant's pass holder`
    `a student's pass holder`
    `a special pass holder`
    `a visit pass holder`
    `a holder of a pass specified by the Minister`

GIVEN `the status` IS A Status, `visit pass validity in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is a tourist` IF
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN `a visit pass holder` THEN `visit pass validity in days` AT MOST 90
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "guiding services" includes "providing any information, description or explanation to the tourist while accompanying the
-- tourist" in or to a place or point of interest, "but not if the information ... is a mere reference to the location of" the place.
GIVEN `accompanying the tourist` IS A BOOLEAN, `a mere reference to location` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the explanation is guiding services` IF
    `accompanying the tourist` AND (NOT `a mere reference to location`)

§§ `20(2), 22 -- remuneration and its presumption`

-- s 20(2): services are for remuneration "if the individual receives or reasonably expects to receive any payment ..., regardless
-- of who makes or is liable to make the payment or where or when".
-- s 22: an individual who provides guiding services "to 8 or more tourists is presumed, unless the contrary is proved," to do so for
-- remuneration if the tourists and the individual are, have been or will be conveyed "in a motor vehicle (other than an omnibus)".
GIVEN `receives or expects payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of tourists` IS A NUMBER, `conveyed in a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the vehicle is an omnibus` IS A BOOLEAN, `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the guiding is treated as for remuneration` IF
        `receives or expects payment`
    OR  (     `number of tourists` AT LEAST 8
          AND `conveyed in a motor vehicle`
          AND (NOT `the vehicle is an omnibus`)
          AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`))

§§ `21 -- licence required`

-- s 21(1): an individual must not act, offer to act, or advertise as a tourist guide "unless he or she holds a valid tourist guide
-- licence". s 20(3): while a licence is suspended the holder is "deemed to be a person who does not hold a valid" licence.
-- (2) not applicable to "(a) the owner or operator of a place or point of interest who himself or herself guides tourists at that
-- place or point" or "(b) any person who is employed or engaged ... by the owner or operator ... to guide tourists at that place".
-- s 43: the Board may, with the Minister's approval, by order in the Gazette exempt any person or class.
-- (3) fine up to $5,000; "second or subsequent offence" up to $10,000.
GIVEN `acts or offers to act as a tourist guide` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the licence is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `owner or operator guiding at own place` IS A BOOLEAN, `engaged by the owner to guide at that place` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exempted by order under s 43` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `guiding without a licence is an offence` IF
        `acts or offers to act as a tourist guide`
    AND (NOT (`holds a licence` AND (NOT `the licence is suspended`)))
    AND (NOT `owner or operator guiding at own place`)
    AND (NOT `engaged by the owner to guide at that place`)
    AND (NOT `exempted by order under s 43`)

GIVEN `a previous conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed guiding` MEANS
    IF `a previous conviction` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

-- s 21(4): any person who "directly or indirectly, employs, engages or otherwise uses the services of an unlicensed tourist guide"
-- (a) "whom the person knows or ought reasonably to know is an unlicensed tourist guide" or (b) "with reckless disregard" -- same
-- fines as (3).
GIVEN `uses the services of the guide` IS A BOOLEAN, `the guide is unlicensed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knows or ought reasonably to know` IS A BOOLEAN, `reckless disregard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using an unlicensed guide is an offence` IF
        `uses the services of the guide`
    AND `the guide is unlicensed`
    AND (`knows or ought reasonably to know` OR `reckless disregard`)

§§ `25(4) -- badge surrender`

-- s 25(4): failing to surrender (or destroy) a badge as required -- fine up to $5,000 "and, in the case of a continuing offence, to
-- a further fine not exceeding $100 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for not surrendering a badge` MEANS
    5000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `28 -- suspension, revocation and lesser sanctions`

-- s 28(1): the Board may suspend "for a period not exceeding 6 months" (or a longer prescribed period), or revoke, if the licensee
-- among other grounds "(e) has committed any offence under any written law punishable with a term of imprisonment exceeding
-- one month". (Other grounds -- false information, contraventions, unfitness, incapacity -- are not modelled.)
GIVEN `maximum imprisonment for the offence in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is a ground to suspend or revoke` IF
    `maximum imprisonment for the offence in months` GREATER THAN 1

GIVEN `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is within the unprescribed limit` IF
    `months of suspension` AT MOST 6

-- s 28(2)(f): instead of suspending or revoking, the Board may "require the licensee to pay a financial penalty of an amount not
-- exceeding $1,000"; (3) that "does not apply in respect of any contravention which is prescribed to be an offence".
GIVEN `the penalty amount` IS A NUMBER, `the contravention is prescribed to be an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may impose the financial penalty` IF
    `the penalty amount` AT MOST 1000 AND (NOT `the contravention is prescribed to be an offence`)

-- s 28(4A)(c): the notice of intended action must give a time "being at least 14 days after the date of service" for representations.
GIVEN `days allowed for representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice allows enough time` IF
    `days allowed for representations` AT LEAST 14

§§ `42A(1) -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 42A(1): an aggrieved person "may appeal to the Minister within 14 days after notice of the decision is served on the person or
-- such extended period as the Minister may allow in any particular case". (Decisions listed in (2) include refusing a licence,
-- suspension or revocation, financial penalties and debarment.) An extension of 0 means none was allowed.
GIVEN `days after notice served` IS A NUMBER, `extended period allowed by the Minister` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days after notice served` AT MOST 14 OR `days after notice served` AT MOST `extended period allowed by the Minister`

§§ `29A -- cruise terminal licence`

-- s 29A(1): "A person must not operate any cruise terminal unless the person has in force a cruise terminal licence"; (2) fine up to
-- $500,000 and "a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day" the offence continues after conviction.
GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for an unlicensed cruise terminal` MEANS
    500000 PLUS 5000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `29R, 29W -- controllers of a cruise terminal licensee`

-- s 29W: a "5% controller" (25%, 50%) is a person who, alone or with associates, "holds 5% or more of the total equity interests in"
-- or "is in a position to control 5% or more of the voting power in" the licensee.
-- s 29R(1): a person must not "(a) become a 5% controller ... without giving written notice to the Controller" -- (2) "within 7 days
-- after"; or "(b) become a 25% controller, a 50% controller or an indirect controller ... without obtaining the prior written approval
-- of the Controller". (8) fine up to $100,000 or imprisonment up to 3 years or both.
DECLARE ControllerStep IS ONE OF
    `nothing required`
    `written notice within 7 days`
    `prior written approval`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `equity percent` IS A NUMBER, `voting percent` IS A NUMBER, `becomes an indirect controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ControllerStep
`what the acquirer must do` MEANS
    IF `becomes an indirect controller` OR `the larger of` `equity percent` `voting percent` AT LEAST 25
    THEN `prior written approval`
    ELSE IF `the larger of` `equity percent` `voting percent` AT LEAST 5
         THEN `written notice within 7 days`
         ELSE `nothing required`

-- s 29R(9): a defence if the person proves "(a) the person was not aware of the contravention when it occurred; (b) ... within 14
-- days after becoming aware ... notified the Controller"; and (c) where a direction was issued under s 29T, complied with it in time
-- or the period has not expired. (11) otherwise lack of intent or knowledge "is not a defence".
GIVEN `was unaware when it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN, `days from awareness to notifying` IS A NUMBER, `a direction was issued` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `complied with the direction or time not expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unawareness defence is made out` IF
        `was unaware when it occurred`
    AND `days from awareness to notifying` AT MOST 14
    AND ((NOT `a direction was issued`) OR `complied with the direction or time not expired`)

§§ `37 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 37(1): "No liability shall lie personally against any member, officer or employee of the Board ... who, acting in good faith and
-- with reasonable care, does or omits to do anything in the execution or purported execution of this Act".
GIVEN `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is personally protected` IF
    `in good faith` AND `with reasonable care`

§§ `39 -- the Merlion symbol`

-- s 39: any person who "without the permission of the Board, uses the Merlion symbol ... or a symbol or representation so nearly
-- resembling the Merlion symbol as to cause confusion" -- fine up to $2,000 or imprisonment up to 6 months or both.
GIVEN `uses the Merlion` IS A BOOLEAN, `uses a confusingly similar symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Board's permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use of the Merlion is an offence` IF
    (`uses the Merlion` OR `uses a confusingly similar symbol`) AND (NOT `has the Board's permission`)

§§ `41 -- composition`

-- s 41(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of
-- the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence" and (b) "$2,000". (1A): the Controller may compound a prescribed Part 3AA
-- offence for "a sum not exceeding $5,000".
GIVEN `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER, `compounded by the Controller under Part 3AA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap` MEANS
    IF `compounded by the Controller under Part 3AA` THEN 5000
    ELSE IF `the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2 AT MOST 2000 THEN `the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2
         ELSE 2000
